00:04:23,636 --> 00:04:29,636
Everybody runs.

2
00:08:47,272 --> 00:08:53,272
Minority Report is a science fiction, action,
thriller film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:13:10,909 --> 00:13:16,909
John Anderton is a top 'Precrime' cop in the late-21st century, when
technology can predict crimes before they're committed.

4
00:17:34,545 --> 00:17:40,545
But Anderton becomes the quarry when another
investigator targets him for a murder charge.

5
00:21:58,181 --> 00:22:04,181
Chief John Anderton, played by Tom Cruise.

6
00:26:21,818 --> 00:26:27,818
Agatha, played by Samantha Morton.

7
00:30:45,454 --> 00:30:51,454
Danny Witwer, played by Colin Farrell.

8
00:35:09,090 --> 00:35:15,090
Director Lamar Burgess, played by Max von Sydow.

9
00:39:32,727 --> 00:39:38,727
Lara Clarke, played by Kathryn Morris.

10
00:43:56,363 --> 00:44:02,363
Jad, played by Steve Harris.

11
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:26,000
Minority Report is a 2002 American science fiction action thriller film directed by Steven Spielberg
and written by Scott Frank and Jon Cohen, who loosely based the screenplay on Philip K.

12
00:52:43,636 --> 00:52:49,636
Dick's 1956 novella "The Minority Report".

13
00:57:07,272 --> 00:57:13,272
It stars Tom Cruise, Colin Farrell, Samantha Morton, and Max von Sydow.

14
01:01:30,909 --> 01:01:36,909
The film takes place in 2054 in the Washington metropolitan area, where a specialized police "precrime" department
apprehends would-be criminals with the use of foreknowledge provided by three psychics called "precogs".

15
01:05:54,545 --> 01:06:00,545
Minority Report combines elements of the action, sci-fi, tech noir, thriller, and whodunit genres, in addition to being a
traditional chase film, with the main protagonist accused of a crime he has not committed and becoming a fugitive.

16
01:10:18,181 --> 01:10:24,181
Spielberg characterized the story as "50% character and 50% very complicated
storytelling with layers and layers of murder mystery and plot".

17
01:14:41,818 --> 01:14:47,818
The film was first optioned in 1992 as a sequel to another Dick adaptation, Total
Recall (1990), with Arnold Schwarzenegger set to reprise his role.

18
01:19:05,454 --> 01:19:11,454
When Carolco Pictures filed for bankruptcy, the film
was reworked into a standalone project.

19
01:23:29,090 --> 01:23:35,090
Its development started in 1997 after Cohen's
script reached Spielberg and Cruise.

20
01:27:52,727 --> 01:27:58,727
Production suffered multiple delays due to Spielberg's work on A.I.

21
01:32:16,363 --> 01:32:22,363
and Cruise's work on Mission: Impossible 2, both of which ran over schedule.

22
01:36:40,000 --> 01:36:46,000
Spielberg consulted scientists in an attempt to present a more plausible future world than that seen in
other sci-fi films, and some of the film's portrayed technology has proven prescient.

23
01:41:03,636 --> 01:41:09,636
It was produced by 20th Century Fox, DreamWorks Pictures, Cruise/Wagner
Productions, Amblin Entertainment, and Blue Tulip Productions.

24
01:45:27,272 --> 01:45:33,272
20th Century Fox and DreamWorks shared distribution duties.

25
01:49:50,909 --> 01:49:56,909
The high-profile collaboration between Spielberg and Cruise made
Minority Report one of 2002's most anticipated films.

26
01:54:14,545 --> 01:54:20,545
It received positive reviews from critics and was a commercial success,
becoming the year's 10th most successful film worldwide.

27
01:58:38,181 --> 01:58:44,181
It grossed over $358 million on a budget of $102 million.

28
02:03:01,818 --> 02:03:07,818
It was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Sound Editing and won four Saturn Awards (Best Science
Fiction Film, Best Direction, Best Writing, and Best Supporting Actress) from 11 nominations.

29
02:07:25,454 --> 02:07:31,454
It has since been included in lists of the greatest
science fiction films of all time.

30
02:11:49,090 --> 02:11:55,090
The film spawned a tie-in video game in 2002 and a
single-season television series in 2015.

31
02:16:12,727 --> 02:16:18,727
The film explores themes of washington dc, usa, police
chief, precognition, hologram, futuristic.

32
02:20:36,363 --> 02:20:42,363
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
